SUMMARY:Asheville Symphony Presents - Masterworks 2: Nightfall
DESCRIPTION:Two performances\, 2 p.m. and 8 p.m. Event Details and Tickets\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSATURDAY\, SEPTEMBER 26\, 2026\n2:00 P.M. AND 8:00 P.M.\nFIRST BAPTIST CHURCH OF ASHEVILLE \nDarko Butorac\, conductor\nJoseph Conyers\, double bass\n  \n\n\n\n\nThere is a serene kind of beauty found only at twilight\, when the landscape cedes to legend; this program lingers in these wild places at their most untamed and fragile. Anna Clyne’s stormy nocturne gathers “every shred of the luminous past” like “a naked woman running mad through the pure night.” Tan Dun’s spiritually cinematic Wolf Totem summons the mythical Mongolian wolf from the grasslands. Sibelius’s devastating Fifth conjures the inscrutable patterns of the aurora. Three works that find beauty in loss\, solace in vast spaces\, and mystery in the gathering dark. \nClyne: This Midnight Hour\nTan: Contrabass Concerto: Wolf Totem\nSibelius: Symphony No. 5
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/asheville-symphony-presents-masterworks-2-nightfall/
LOCATION:First Baptist Church of Asheville
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
GEO:35.5988729;-82.5474388
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR